{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793704335,"nonce":"JTykepO/sOAA8SQo89KVCox+ovY=","message":"F3 follow-up (uncommitted): flows did not animate without input once the element path was gone, because nothing asked the window loop for frames. Added a loop driver: FlowShader::animated (the shader reads time or frame_index, set at codegen), Canvas::flow_loop(FlowLoop::{Auto, Always, Never, While(f), Clock(FlowClock)}), and FlowClock (playing/paused, play, pause, seek, step(dt), set_rate) so code can step a shader programmatically. A canvas calls request_animation_tick per paint while its loop wants frames, so frames stop when the canvas is not painted. Checked live: flow_demo animates with no input. Tests: blinc_layout/tests/flow_loop.rs and flow_clock unit tests.","files":null}]}